WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.640
From consultation to neat, comfortable cornrows.

2
00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:08.000
This is the video for module two of Hair Care and Simple Styling.

3
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:19.210
Good stylists ask the right questions first, so there are no surprises. Ask what style, size and length she wants, and agree what is realistic for her hair.

4
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:28.480
Ask about her last relaxer, colour or keratin treatment. A chemical service in the last two weeks changes what is safe.

5
00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:34.910
Ask about itching, tenderness, and past reactions to extension hair or products.

6
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:40.750
Ask how long she will keep the style. That guides braid size and aftercare.

7
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:51.580
Then say the price clearly, whether it includes extension hair, and roughly how many hours it will take. Write it all on a client card, and keep it private.

8
00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:57.950
Start with clean, moisturised, stretched hair, and the client's head at your chest height.

9
00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:06.660
Step one. With the comb tail, part a straight line from the hairline to the nape, then a second line parallel to it. Clip the rest away.

10
00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:13.330
Step two. A little gel or braiding cream along the row controls frizz and gives grip.

11
00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:20.020
Step three. At the hairline, take a small piece and divide it into three equal strands.

12
00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:30.190
Step four. Cross the left strand under the middle, then the right strand under the new middle. This underhand method makes the classic raised cornrow.

13
00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:38.820
Step five. Before each cross, pick up a little loose hair from the row with your index finger and add it to the outer strand.

14
00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:45.980
Keep those amounts small and equal. Picking up too much is why rows get wider towards the nape.

15
00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:56.320
Step six. Keep your knuckles close to the scalp to avoid gaps and loops. At the nape, finish with a normal three-strand braid and secure the end.

16
00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:05.720
A cornrow should feel snug. Pull hardest in the middle of the head, and be gentlest at the hairline and temples, where hair is finest.

17
00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:14.480
If she winces, if you see small white bumps, or the scalp lifts like a tent around the braid, it is too tight. Loosen it.

18
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:21.820
Repeated tight styling can cause traction alopecia, hair loss from constant pulling, which can become permanent.

19
00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:32.500
For example, Halima in Kano has a client at 10 a.m. for medium knotless braids. Consultation and scalp check take 10 minutes.

20
00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:37.680
Stretching with leave-in and a blow dryer on medium takes 40 minutes.

21
00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:44.990
About 120 braids at roughly 2 minutes each is 240 minutes, or 4 hours.

22
00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.290
Sealing ends, the final check and aftercare talk take 20 minutes.

23
00:02:51.540 --> 00:03:02.360
That is 310 minutes, about 5 hours 10 minutes. So Halima books her next client for 4 p.m., with time to clean tools, eat and rest her hands.

24
00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:14.060
Check the hairline, crown and nape in good light. If you see signs of infection, open sores or a recent chemical burn, do not continue. Suggest a clinic.

25
00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:23.690
When you seal synthetic ends, dip them in hot water from a stable bowl, never from a kettle held over the client, then blot with a towel.

26
00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:34.800
With children, the parent consults and the child's comfort comes first. Choose bigger, lighter styles. If a child cries from pain, the braid is too tight.

27
00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:45.780
It's fine teaches you nothing. After each practice, take photos, time yourself, and score parts, braid size, comfort and ends from 1 to 5.

28
00:03:47.030 --> 00:04:01.410
For example, Rukayat in Abeokuta scored her parts 2 out of 5. She practised parting on a mannequin for 20 minutes a day. In three sessions her total rose from 12 to 17 out of 20, and she saved an hour.

29
00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:15.070
To remember. Consult and write a card every time. Stretch before parting. Pick up small, equal amounts for even rows. Firm but never painful. And fix one weak point at a time.

30
00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:25.390
Now practise. Run one real consultation, braid a full all-back with a comfort rating, and score a section of twists or box braids.

31
00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.680
Continue with the lessons below.
